  "no_authority": {
    "ArchitecturePageSchema": "`PaginatedResponse[ArchitectureResponse]` is a generic envelope shared by many routes; its item type is covered by `ArchitectureSchema` above. The envelope's own three fields are pagination, not payload.",
    "DecisionRefusalSchema": "Mirrors what `_bounded_decision_detail` writes into a failed job's detail. That is a dict built in a service, not a declared model.",
    "GenerateAsyncSchema": "`POST /chat/generate-async` is annotated `-> dict[str, object]` and declares no `response_model`.",
    "JobProgressSchema": "`progress` is free-form by design \u2014 the connector reads one nested key out of it and types the rest `unknown`. There is no model, and there should not be.",
    "JobSchema": "`GET /chat/jobs/{job_id}` is annotated `-> dict[str, object]` and declares no `response_model`. `schemas/jobs.py` has a `JobHistoryItem`, but it is the *list* row and carries different fields; treating it as the authority here would produce false failures.",
    "ProjectListSchema": "Same route. The `{projects, total, page, page_size}` envelope is assembled inline in `app/http/projects/handlers.py`, not by a model.",
    "ProjectSchema": "Neither `GET /projects/` nor `GET /projects/{project_id}` declares a `response_model`, and `handle_list_projects` returns a plain dict. `schemas/projects.py` defines a `ProjectResponse`, but these routes do not use it, so diffing against it would assert a contract the API does not actually keep."
  }
